    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "6c0a87ae-1af3-3d0e-99e6-08aaabef2f3e",
                "word": "dyspepsia",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "9fce25ef-1da4-4d00-84b3-0b49d94b6514",
                        "entry_id": "6c0a87ae-1af3-3d0e-99e6-08aaabef2f3e",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "dyspepsias"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9bebf63a-9ce5-3997-84f6-47bfd1580e2e",
                        "entry_id": "6c0a87ae-1af3-3d0e-99e6-08aaabef2f3e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Any mild disorder of digestion characterised by stomach pain, discomfort, heartburn, and nausea, often following a meal."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c59d7b03-2e38-49fa-9c37-5b6019e68f34",
                                "sense_id": "9bebf63a-9ce5-3997-84f6-47bfd1580e2e",
                                "text": "He divides dyspepsias into accidental, temporary (indigestions) and habitual."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "593ed4d6-e557-4ddb-bae8-a4036a46bd47",
                                "sense_id": "9bebf63a-9ce5-3997-84f6-47bfd1580e2e",
                                "text": "It is not my strength of mind (exert it as I may) that will prevent me from experiencing dyspepsia, if such follies as these are exhibited before me."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0566ac57-2c34-41e3-93b7-230640d0dc9f",
                                "sense_id": "9bebf63a-9ce5-3997-84f6-47bfd1580e2e",
                                "text": "\"And the cramps when my body - like a badly articulated skeleton - would all get twisted into one rigid tangle! But now, except some dyspepsia and urticaria of the palms, I am free from pain.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8010b2bb-d618-48b7-9123-26f0adecae60",
                                "sense_id": "9bebf63a-9ce5-3997-84f6-47bfd1580e2e",
                                "text": "I've never hunted myself, but I understand that half the battle is being able to make noises like some jungle animal with dyspepsia, and I believe that Aunt Dahlia in her prime could lift fellow-members of the Quorn and Pytchley out of their saddles with a single yip, though separated from them by two ploughed fields and a spinney."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fd35ad17-a091-4113-ad3b-69ff9767d373",
                        "source_entry_id": "6c0a87ae-1af3-3d0e-99e6-08aaabef2f3e",
                        "source_sense_id": "9bebf63a-9ce5-3997-84f6-47bfd1580e2e",
                        "source_sense_description": "pathology: disorder of digestion",
                        "target_lang_word": "indigestie",
                        "target_lang_code": "nl",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "indigestie",
                                "target_lang_code": "nl",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2c6266b9-6789-3ce0-ae9a-5996326d03f2",
                                        "entry_id": "b207a6af-abf5-30ab-bee0-666205f9b908",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "ziek worden door te veel en te snel te eten"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "12b1c9bb-a6a9-4e55-b4eb-ff792cd36200",
                                                "sense_id": "2c6266b9-6789-3ce0-ae9a-5996326d03f2",
                                                "text": "Indigestie: Dit is het overladen van de maag. Vaak veroorzaakt door te snel en te veel te eten. Vooral moeilijk verteerbaar/vet voedsel wekt dit op. De klachten worden door de aanwezigheid van 'pijn op de borst' of 'achter het borstbeen' gemakkelijk verward met die van een acuut coronair syndroom. Bij twijfel moet een eventuele coronaire oorzaak hiervan worden uitgesloten! Oorzaken van indigestie zijn overeten, te veel alcohol en zuurophoping in de maag."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ae6c3844-9d97-33d4-9456-be08db3675d9",
                                        "entry_id": "b207a6af-abf5-30ab-bee0-666205f9b908",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "een gestoorde spijsvertering in het algemeen"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "985018a8-39be-408b-a712-a374b72bb6a1",
                                                "sense_id": "ae6c3844-9d97-33d4-9456-be08db3675d9",
                                                "text": "Toegegeven, in het hoofd van de ene chef is het fascinerender rondreizen dan in dat van de ander. En wanneer je twee of drie afleveringen achter elkaar kijkt, dreigt het gevaar van indigestie. Hapje voor hapje van genieten dus, en tussendoor rustig laten verteren."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d11437b0-f9cf-43cc-b3ee-d8316438ffd7",
                        "source_entry_id": "6c0a87ae-1af3-3d0e-99e6-08aaabef2f3e",
                        "source_sense_id": "9bebf63a-9ce5-3997-84f6-47bfd1580e2e",
